    ; keeps the list, and a statement a function of its own runs again notes the read; the
    ; function that runs it again, and one that builds an arm or a row of a markup region or what
    ; an element gives a slot, read the local and the list where the function that declares them
    ; keeps them. A read in a `whenever` clause notes nothing: the clause is tested in a live
    ; action as it is subscribed. The reference keeps one list for every local of a function by
